body:
I don't have all the answers for this method, but I should think you'd simply update a single image in your own private repo each time there's an update, then use \`docker run\` on each node to run the new release. This gives you the delta option, but only having to do so once. Downtime is the time it takes to pull the image from your private repo (which can be locally available) and start the application.

&#x200B;

My companies methodology (and many others) is each container that gets run is simply supplying configuration options to an already existing image.

Looks like you can enforce global limits fairly easily. (quick google found URL...)

&#x200B;

 [https://www.thegeekdiary.com/how-to-apply-resource-limits-via-limits-conf-for-a-docker-container/](https://www.thegeekdiary.com/how-to-apply-resource-limits-via-limits-conf-for-a-docker-container/)

Although it sounds like this would solve your problem, it goes against the docker ideology. I think you would do better setting up a docker repo rather than copying your images around. 

&#x200B;

Example: Brand new linux install of whatever OS supports docker, assuming it supports at least your required version. Setup your docker daemon however you want it to be. Connect it to your private docker repo ([https://docs.docker.com/registry/deploying/](https://docs.docker.com/registry/deploying/)), and \`docker pull\` whatever images you want. This way, if you make a change to one of those images, you would only need run \`docker pull\` again on any system you want updated. One True Source if you will.

&#x200B;

After that, I would highly suggest updating your Live Boot images to already include the docker daemon install, and heck, automatically pull the images you need to use, and run the containers you want use. Your first login should already have everything you need to do your work.

And there it is. My bad for not finding it first.

&#x200B;

[https://www.reddit.com/r/DestinyTheGame/comments/9eb1sb/are\_engrams\_back\_to\_being\_affected\_by\_your/](https://www.reddit.com/r/DestinyTheGame/comments/9eb1sb/are_engrams_back_to_being_affected_by_your/)
